    "descriptionChirho": "Called, summoned, invited — a verbal adjective describing those who have been divinely called or appointed. Used in the NT for those called by God to salvation and service (Rom 1:1, 1:6-7, 8:28, 1 Cor 1:1-2, 1:24, Jude 1:1, Rev 17:14). Multilingual evidence is uniform across both clusters: spa 'llamado/llamados', hin 'bulaye hue/bulaya hua' (called ones, sg/pl), arb 'mad'uww/mad'uwwun' (called, sg/pl), kor '부르심 받은' (bureusim badeun, 'having received a calling'), swa 'aliyeitwa/walioitwa' (sg/pl passive forms). The Adj-NMS vs Adj-NMP/Adj-DMP split is purely grammatical number agreement.",
